## Why This Is Asked

Assess system design capabilities for regulated, privacy-sensitive AI copilots in multi-tenant SaaS environments, focusing on data governance, residency requirements, and auditable prompt management.

## Key Concepts

- Multi-tenant isolation with per-tenant data compartments and role-based access control
- Versioned knowledge base stored in Azure Blob Storage and grounded via Cognitive Search
- PII redaction using Text Analytics with policy-based gating mechanisms
- Comprehensive audit trails stored in Data Lake Storage, tamper-evident logging, and Event Hubs for governance events
- Canary deployment strategy behind API Management for controlled rollout

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: Durable Function orchestrates KB grounding and compliance checks
const orchestrator = function* (context) {
  const tenantId = context.bindingData.tenantId;
  const query = context.bindingData.query;

  // Redact PII before processing
  const redactedQuery = await redactPII(query);

  // Ground against versioned KB
  const grounding = await searchKB(redactedQuery, tenantId);

  // Generate compliant response
  const response = await generateResponse(grounding);

  // Audit all interactions
  await auditInteraction(tenantId, query, response);

  return response;
};
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to architect a secure, scalable incident-response automation platform across tenants using Azure AI services. Covers real-time event ingestion, strict data isolation, guardrails for safe prompt generation, canary testing, and comprehensive audit logging.

## Key Concepts
- Real-time Event Hubs ingestion with tenant-scoped event routing
- Tenant-isolated Cognitive Search indexes for grounded KB retrieval
- PII redaction via Text Analytics before processing and storage
- Canary playbook execution behind API Management with traffic splitting policies
- Data Lake for raw audit logs, Cosmos DB for structured remediation results
- Azure AD RBAC for multi-tenant access control

## Code Example
```javascript
// Initialize per-tenant Cognitive Search client with Managed Identity
const { DefaultAzureCredential } = require('@azure/identity');
const { SearchIndexClient } = require('@azure/search-documents');

async function getTenantSearchClient(tenantId) {
  const credential = new DefaultAzureCredential();
  const indexName = `kb-${tenantId}`;
  return new SearchIndexClient(
    `https://${process.env.SEARCH_SERVICE}.search.windows.net/`,
    indexName,
    credential
  );
}
```
